# routing decision snapshot (TASK-110)
# direct = run on the terminal · model = hand the line to the model
# regenerate after an intended heuristic change: UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test routing_decision_snapshot

## looks_like_prose — English starting with a real command word routes to the model, real invocations stay direct
who is zachary hohertz                               -> model   [looks_like_prose]
find me big files                                    -> model   [looks_like_prose]
make this file executable                            -> model   [looks_like_prose]
watch for events from atum, let me know about activity -> model   [looks_like_prose]
find big files, oldest first                         -> model   [looks_like_prose]
who                                                  -> direct  [auto]
who -a                                               -> direct  [auto]
which ls                                             -> direct  [auto]
find . -name foo                                     -> direct  [auto]
tail logfile                                         -> direct  [auto]
echo hello there world                               -> direct  [auto]
cat "my file" backup                                 -> direct  [auto]
watch -n 5 free                                      -> direct  [auto]
tail logs/app.log                                    -> direct  [auto]

## bare-yes guard — a lone confirmation token (y/yes/n/no) routes to the model; multi-word invocations stay direct
yes                                                  -> model   [bare-yes guard]
yes please                                           -> direct  [auto]
yes please thanks                                    -> model   [looks_like_prose]
test -f file                                         -> direct  [auto]
test the connection right now                        -> model   [looks_like_prose]

## !/? force routing — explicit escape hatches override every other heuristic
!who is zachary hohertz                              -> direct  [! force]
!ls -la                                              -> direct  [! force]
?ls                                                  -> model   [? force]
?make this file executable                           -> model   [? force]
?who                                                 -> model   [? force]

## tokenizer gate — shell syntax and prose punctuation the tokenizer rejects route to the model
who is on this machine right now?                    -> model   [shell-syntax / non-tokenizable]
echo *.rs                                            -> model   [shell-syntax / non-tokenizable]
cat a > b                                            -> model   [shell-syntax / non-tokenizable]
